  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run, which used one of the 6 allowed runs. It reported 20 witnesses, 23 names and no compositions.\n\nBefore that run I made two shell calls that weren't the gate command. One was an empty `echo`, and the other, the gate with extra flags, was blocked. Neither ran the gate or changed a file. `task_result.md` notes both.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_500.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject is a vehicle, as the admitted aggregate `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle` defines it.\n- **When it applies:** the subject occupies a travel region governed by one of two signs whose posted conditions hold for it:\n  - a hazardous-place zone sign that starts a zone (not an end sign), or\n  - a no-stopping regulatory sign.\n- **The duty:** in every such region, re-selected the same way, the vehicle must not be at a complete halt (`p.halt_speed_tolerance`). A halt is allowed in two cases:\n  - **Queue:** another road user is ahead in the same lane, with a gap between bodies of at most `p.queue_halt_gap`.\n  - **Device or officer:** a region the vehicle occupies is governed by any of these:\n    - a stop sign or a yield sign;\n    - a signal showing red, yellow, flashing red, or a red or yellow arrow;\n    - a railway signal with lights flashing or gate not up;\n    - a police officer indicating stop.\n- **Choices:** the node left nothing open, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_500.lean`): I built the six planned scenes and added 14 more so that every condition in the rule changes at least one result. Each exception has a passing case, and each sign or signal condition has a failing case. For example, the gate-down case passes and lights dark with gate up fails. A car beside the subject in the next lane, or one ahead but beyond the queue gap, doesn't excuse the halt.\n\n`task_result.md`, in the node's working directory, records the run log, the scene list and why I finished.",
